            "id": 104153,
            "creation_time": "2026-11-10T16:58:16Z",
            "count": 2,
            "text": "After some discussion in R Core, we would prefer not to change this.\n\nNumeric versions are really designed to implement simple variants of\nsemantic versioning, allowing both . and - to separate the numeric\nparts, without having additional semantics (such as separating the\n\"upstream version part\" from the \"local version part\".\n\nIf we changed \n\nR> as.numeric_version(\"1.2\")\n[1] ‘1.2’\nR> as.numeric_version(\"1-2\")\n[1] ‘1.2’\n\nto format/print differently it would be strange to still take them the\nsame for comparisons, and we cannot change that.",
            "bug_id": 19004
          }
        ]
      }
    }
